### What is “good mileage”?

This refers to the mileage on your vehicle at the time of your first repair attempt. Manufacturers are entitled to deduct these miles from your buyback amount.
### Do I need to keep the vehicle?

If your vehicle is from an “Opt-in” manufacturer under the new law from July 2025, then Yes. You must keep the vehicle until the claim is filed and for 60 days after. If you wish to sell, trade, or dispose of it, notify us 60 days in advance. If your vehicle is from an “Opt-out” manufacturer, no you do not need to maintain possession before your case is filed.
